## Standing rules (inherited from GTA6_Stilt_House, never ask again)
- One object `/obj/JapanScene`, subnets `Component_<Name>_<id>`, id at the end.
- Model ISOLATED at the origin, straight and axis aligned : a 3/4 look is the CAMERA, never a rotated model.
- Write `breakdowns/<id>_<Name>_breakdown.md` (sub-components, parts, measures) BEFORE modelling.
- Judge on a 4-view sheet (front, profile, bottom, iso) plus an overlay with the reference image.
- Every dimension is a spare parm on `/obj/JapanScene` (HDA law) ; placement is a separate transform node.
- Symmetry and alignment are MEASURED on the built geometry, never eyeballed.
- Never delete : superseded work is renamed `_blockout` and unplugged.
- Save after each step : `snapshot save` plus the hip.

